<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    DLL-load hardening core for the Windows app (Phase 5 · R19 library-validation equivalent).

    macOS gives the daemon a "library validation" hardened-runtime guarantee: the loader refuses
    to load any code not signed by the app's Team ID. Windows has no single equivalent, so the
    R19 parity is assembled from THREE controls, and this library owns the runtime one:

      1. RUNTIME dll-search hardening (this library): at process start the managed app calls
         SetDefaultDllDirectories(LOAD_LIBRARY_SEARCH_DEFAULT_DIRS) + SetDllDirectory("") to strip
         the current working directory and the legacy unsafe search order from LoadLibrary — the
         classic DLL-planting / DLL-preloading defense.
      2. LINK-TIME hardening (windows/dist/props/OpenBurnBar.Windows.NativeHardening.props): the
         in-tree native binaries link with /DEPENDENTLOADFLAG:0x0800 (LOAD_LIBRARY_SEARCH_SYSTEM32),
         /guard:cf (Control Flow Guard), /HIGHENTROPYVA, /DYNAMICBASE, /NXCOMPAT.
      3. PE hardening for the managed app (OpenBurnBar.Windows.Hardening.props): HighEntropyVA +
         deterministic build so the shipped EXE gets full ASLR entropy.

    HardeningPolicy below is the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for the required flags/properties; the
    test suite (windows/tests/dist) asserts the .props files actually carry them, so the policy
    and the packaging props can never silently drift.

    The DllImport declarations compile on any host (they are just P/Invoke metadata); they only
    EXECUTE on Windows (guarded by OperatingSystem.IsWindows()), so this restores + is unit-tested
    on the macOS authoring host today. net8.0, no Windows TFM.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <RootNamespace>OpenBurnBar.Dist.Hardening</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>OpenBurnBar.Dist.Hardening</AssemblyName>
    <!-- Silence the CA1416 platform-compat analyzer: every Win32 call is guarded by an
         OperatingSystem.IsWindows() check at runtime, which the analyzer cannot see across
         the P/Invoke boundary. The guard IS present (see DllSearchHardening.Apply). -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CA1416</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="OpenBurnBar.Dist.Hardening.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
